<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<chapter xml:id="ch18-generalized-stokes" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>The Generalized Stokes Theorem</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>Chapters 16 and 17 supplied forms, their integrals, and their exterior derivatives. We now specify the orientation induced on a boundary and state the theorem relating a boundary integral to an integral of the derivative inside. The familiar Fundamental Theorem of Calculus, Green, Stokes, and divergence theorems are its low-dimensional cases; the proof section distinguishes exact coordinate calculations from the general patching argument.</p>
  </introduction>

